<title>NORWAY: DnB Q1 pre-tax profit rises 7 pct.</title>
<headline>DnB Q1 pre-tax profit rises 7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31.</p>
<p>					(millions of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>Net interest income			     1,054   vs   1,069</p>
<p>Other operating income			    856   vs     673</p>
<p>Operating expenses				1,127   vs   1,121</p>
<p>Pre-tax operating profit before losses	784   vs     621</p>
<p>Net loss/reversals on loans, guarantees	43   vs     149</p>
<p>Pre-tax operating profit			  826   vs     771</p>
<p>Taxes						     6   vs	 6</p>
<p>Net profit					    820   vs     766</p>
<p>Net profit from Vital Forsikring		 67   vs	25</p>
<p>Commission and fee income			 441   vs     382</p>
<p>Commission expenses and fees paid		82   vs	76</p>
<p>Net profit on foreign exchange and</p>
<p>		    financial instruments	 325   vs     208</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of Norway's largest bank is Den norske Bank ASA (DnB). A Reuter poll of seven analysts forecast a pre-tax operating profit of 698 million crowns and a net interest income of 1.09 billion crowns.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
